00:00:00,158 --> 00:00:09,359
truth. CHAPTER 6 THERE WAS someone CRYING— —THERE WAS!" The next day the rain poured down in

2
00:00:09,359 --> 00:00:14,079
torrents again, and when Mary looked out of her window the Moore was almost

3
00:00:14,079 --> 00:00:19,238
hidden by gray mist and cloud. There could be no going out

4
00:00:19,238 --> 00:00:25,399
today What do you do in your cottage when it rains like this?" she asked Martha.

5
00:00:25,399 --> 00:00:29,238
"Try to keep from under each other's feet mostly," Martha

6
00:00:29,238 --> 00:00:35,118
answered hey there does seem a lot of us then. Mother's a good-tempered woman but

7
00:00:35,118 --> 00:00:41,399
she gets fair moyed The biggest ones goes out in the Cow Shed and plays there

8
00:00:41,399 --> 00:00:46,238
dick and he doesn't mind the wet. He goes out just the same as if the sun was

9
00:00:46,238 --> 00:00:50,920
shining He says he sees things on rainy days as doesn't show when it's fair

10
00:00:50,920 --> 00:00:56,118
weather. He once found a little fox cub half drowned in its hole ho and he

11
00:00:56,118 --> 00:00:59,118
brought it home in the bosom of his shirt to keep it

12
